Backstage Coding changed the compilation by joining exact numeric NPC IDs and
exact observed names across vendors, NPC interactions and creature reactions,
requiring Merchant evidence, and retaining bounded factual listings, contributor
counts, dates, approximate player interaction points and whether the merchant
window offered repairs. Each build is normalized separately, then merged
newest-first: sellers join by exact ID (newest build's name wins); positions,
listings (by exact key) and observed reaction values are unioned with exact
dedupe and bounded caps; lastSeen is the latest date and sources the largest
single-build count; repairs is kept when any build observed it. Dropped counts
are per-build dropped rows, summed. Prices, stock, raw side, narrative and world
coordinates are omitted. Reactions are historical observations for the named
faction, never proof of current access or purchase availability.
Unknown factions and multiple-map mobile observations remain browse-only.
Sources count contributing saved files, not observations. See source-lock.json
for immutable input URLs, bytes, hashes, metadata and compiled artifact checksum.

